course: dictionary
lesson: 14461
title: Parisian: from Paris
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Parisian is about Paris, the capital city of France. As an adjective it tells you a thing is from Paris or connected with Paris. «She sat at a small Parisian café and ordered a hot chocolate.» The word Parisian tells you where the café is.
explain: Look inside the word: Paris is at the start of Parisian, so the word is about Paris. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in Paris to check. «A Paris café» still makes sense, so Parisian means from Paris.
explain: Parisian can also be a noun, meaning a person who lives in Paris or comes from there. «Mum said the Parisians love their city.» Parisians means more than one person. Always write Parisian with a capital P, just like Paris and French.
fact: Parisian means from or connected with Paris, the capital city of France.
fact: As a noun, a Parisian is a person who lives in Paris or comes from there. The plural is Parisians.
fact: Parisian is always written with a capital P, just like «Paris» and «French».
fact: Examples of Parisian things are a Parisian café and the Parisian Metro, which are both in Paris.
fact: Paris is in France, and the Eiffel Tower and the River Seine are famous places there.
exercise: «She sat at a small Parisian café and ordered a hot chocolate.» What does Parisian mean here? | Made of wood | From Spain | *From or connected with Paris | Very small
exercise: «Mum said the Parisians are very proud of their city.» Who are the Parisians? | The French words in a book | Cafés near the river | Ben and his dog | *People who live in Paris or come from there
exercise: Which of these is a Parisian thing? | *A café in the streets of Paris | A bowl of porridge from Glasgow | A sandwich from London | A kangaroo from Australia
test: «The Parisian Metro was busy with tourists.» What does Parisian tell you about the Metro? | It is in Spain | Its colour | It is very old | *It is in Paris
test: «Lucas hopes to meet a Parisian in the park.» What is a Parisian? | *A person who lives in Paris or comes from there | A kind of bread | A street in London | A French cake
exam: «The Parisian children talked about the River Seine and the Eiffel Tower.» Which meaning of Parisian fits best here? | Very loud | From Italy | Old and ruined | *From or connected with Paris
